<LegalLayout
  title="Cookie Policy — ImgFeel"
  description="Learn about the cookies and browser storage technologies used on ImgFeel, their purposes, advertising disclosures, and how to manage or disable them."
  canonicalUrl="https://imgfeel.com/cookie-policy/"
>
  <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
  <p class="last-updated"><strong>Last Updated:</strong> August 16, 2026</p>

  <h2>1. What Are Cookies?</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies are small data files stored directly on your computer, tablet, or smartphone when you visit a website. They are widely used by web developers to make websites function properly, enhance user experience, and provide analytical or advertising data to website operators.
  </p>
  <p>
    In addition to cookies, modern websites may utilize similar browser storage technologies, such as <strong>Local Storage</strong> and <strong>Session Storage</strong>, which allow small amounts of data to be saved locally within your browser without being transmitted to servers on every network request.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Types of Cookies Used on ImgFeel</h2>
  <p>ImgFeel utilizes cookies and browser storage for specific, well-defined functions:</p>

  <h3>A. Strictly Essential & Functional Cookies</h3>
  <p>
    These cookies and local storage items are essential for the website to function smoothly. They remember your interactive tool configurations, such as your chosen units (cm vs mm), output format selections, or theme preferences. These do not store personal information and do not track you across other websites.
  </p>

  <h3>B. Performance & Analytics Cookies</h3>
  <p>
    We may use privacy-respecting analytics services (such as Google Analytics or Cloudflare Web Analytics) that place cookies to gather aggregate, anonymized data about how visitors interact with ImgFeel. This includes metrics such as page load speed, session counts, and tool popularity. This information helps us optimize tool performance and identify bugs.
  </p>

  <h3>C. Advertising & Google AdSense Cookies</h3>
  <p>
    To keep our image tools free for everyone without subscription fees, ImgFeel may display third-party advertisements via <strong>Google AdSense</strong> and authorized advertising partners.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Google uses cookies (such as the DoubleClick cookie) to serve ads based on your visit to ImgFeel and other websites across the web.</li>
    <li>These cookies allow ad networks to provide relevant advertising, prevent the same advertisement from appearing repeatedly, and measure the effectiveness of ad campaigns.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Third-Party Cookies on Our Site</h2>
  <p>
    Some cookies are placed by third-party services that appear on our pages. Third-party providers (such as Google for advertising and analytics) manage their own cookies according to their respective privacy policies. ImgFeel does not have direct access to or control over the cookies used by third-party advertisers.
  </p>

  <h2>4. What We Do NOT Use Cookies For</h2>
  <p>To ensure complete clarity regarding our image processing privacy:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>We <strong>never</strong> use cookies or local storage to capture, store, or transmit your images.</li>
    <li>We <strong>never</strong> store sensitive personal financial or identity information in cookies.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. How You Can Manage or Disable Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    You have full control over the cookies saved on your device. You can modify your browser settings to accept, reject, or delete cookies at any time.
  </p>

  <h3>Browser-Specific Cookie Controls:</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google Chrome:</strong> Settings → Privacy and security → Cookies and other site data</li>
    <li><strong>Mozilla Firefox:</strong> Settings → Privacy & Security → Cookies and Site Data</li>
    <li><strong>Apple Safari:</strong> Preferences → Privacy → Manage Website Data</li>
    <li><strong>Microsoft Edge:</strong> Settings → Cookies and site permissions → Manage and delete cookies and site data</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Opting Out of Targeted & Behavioral Advertising:</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google Ads Settings:</strong> You can manage personalized advertising preferences at <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://adssettings.google.com/</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Digital Advertising Alliance (US):</strong> You can opt out of interest-based ads from participating companies at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.aboutads.info/choices</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>European Interactive Digital Advertising Alliance (EU/EEA):</strong> You can opt out at <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.youronlinechoices.eu</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Network Advertising Initiative (NAI):</strong> You can opt out at <a href="https://optout.networkadvertising.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://optout.networkadvertising.org/</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Updates to This Cookie Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may periodically update this Cookie Policy to reflect technical, operational, or legal changes. Any modifications will be posted here with an updated "Last Updated" date.
  </p>

